    "brief": "Kit's maker space has a microcontroller whose pin gives 5 V through 25 ohm and must never give more than 20 mA here. It has to switch a 12 V fan (60 ohm and a 10 mH winding: 200 mA). A pin cannot do that alone, so a transistor does the heavy lifting: the pin gives a small base current and the transistor lets a hundred times more through the fan. The fan must see at least 11.0 V with the pin high and at most 0.5 V with it low, and the bench also switches it on and off at 100 Hz.",
