        "done": false,
        "id": "base",
        "optional": false,
        "shown": false,
        "target": "pad:2,7",
        "text": "A resistor goes from the PIN pad to the transistor's base: it sets how much base current the pin gives."
      },
      {
        "done": false,
        "id": "wire",
        "optional": false,
        "shown": false,
        "target": "pad:22,4",
        "text": "Wire the PIN pad through the resistor to the base, the emitter to GND and the collector to the COLL pad (the fan's low end)."
      },
      {
        "done": false,
        "id": "diode",
        "optional": true,
        "shown": false,
        "target": "box:1n4007",
        "text": "A diode across the fan, its banded end on the 12 V side, gives the fan's current somewhere to go when the transistor turns off."
      },
      {
        "done": false,
        "id": "diode-burn",
        "optional": false,
        "shown": false,
        "target": "box:1n4007",
        "text": "The transistor burned when the fan switched off: a fan is a coil, and a coil's current cannot stop at once. Put a diode across the fan, its banded end on the 12 V side, before you try again."
      },
      {
        "done": false,
        "id": "power",
        "optional": false,
        "shown": false,
        "target": "rocker",
